## NON-NEGOTIABLE HONESTY RULES (apply to every page, component, API and test)
1. Never fabricate diagnostic results, sensor readings, health scores, accuracy figures or trends. Show proper empty states when there is no data.
2. If no trained model is configured, the analysis returns the status `model_not_configured` and the UI shows **"AI model not configured"** or **"Analysis unavailable"**. Never a fake prediction.
3. Any demo or illustrative content must carry a visible **"Sample data"** badge and live only in a clearly separated `/src/demo` folder, switchable by `VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_DATA=true`. Default is `false`.
4. Do not show a numeric "Vehicle Health Score" until a validated scoring method exists. Show model-supported classifications and observations instead. Include a disabled placeholder card explaining why.
5. Fault-specific classes (engine, chain/sprocket, valve, bearing, idle, exhaust) are displayed only if the model response explicitly lists them as validated in its `supported_classes` metadata. Otherwise only "Normal pattern" vs "Abnormal pattern" is shown.
6. Smartphone motion sensors measure the phone's motion, not engine vibration directly. Wherever sensor graphs appear, add a short note saying so and that mounting position affects interpretation.
7. Always visually and textually separate **AI-generated observations** (labelled "AI observation – not a diagnosis") from **mechanic-confirmed diagnoses** (labelled "Mechanic confirmed", with mechanic name and date).
8. Do not claim the Android app is connected, the AI is trained, or fault detection works until that part is actually implemented and tested. Report remaining work explicitly in the README under "Known gaps / remaining integration work".
9. Never put service-role keys or secrets in browser code. Use only `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` in the frontend.

