## DATABASE (Supabase PostgreSQL) — write full migration SQL
Use `uuid` primary keys (`gen_random_uuid()`), `created_at` / `updated_at` (timestamptz, trigger-maintained), and `user_id` ownership on all tables.

Tables:
- **profiles**(id = auth.users.id, display_name, avatar_url, created_at, updated_at)
- **vehicles**(id, user_id, nickname, make, model, year, registration_identifier nullable, notes, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at nullable)
- **inspection_sessions**(id, user_id, vehicle_id, client_session_id (unique per user, for idempotent Android uploads), started_at, ended_at, duration_seconds, source enum[`android`,`web_upload`], recording_config jsonb, sensor_availability jsonb, status enum[`created`,`uploading`,`uploaded`,`validated`,`processing`,`processed`,`failed`], notes)
- **audio_recordings**(id, session_id, user_id, storage_path, sample_rate, channels, duration_seconds, size_bytes, sha256, input_device_info jsonb, created_at)
- **sensor_recordings**(id, session_id, user_id, sensor_type enum[`accelerometer`,`gyroscope`], storage_path, sample_count, nominal_rate_hz, size_bytes, sha256, created_at)
- **analysis_results**(id, session_id, user_id, status enum[`queued`,`running`,`completed`,`failed`,`unavailable`], result_category, confidence numeric nullable, uncertainty jsonb nullable, supported_classes jsonb, class_probabilities jsonb nullable, model_name, model_version, preprocessing_version, feature_summary jsonb, quality_observations jsonb, recommendation text, error_code, started_at, completed_at)
- **mechanic_confirmations**(id, user_id, vehicle_id, session_id nullable, component, diagnosis_text, mechanic_name, confirmed_on, created_at)
- **maintenance_events**(id, user_id, vehicle_id, event_date, event_type, description, mileage_km nullable, performed_by, mechanic_notes, created_at)
- **shared_reports**(id, user_id, session_id, token_hash unique, expires_at nullable, revoked_at nullable, options jsonb, view_count, last_viewed_at, created_at)

Add indexes on every foreign key, `(user_id, created_at desc)`, `(vehicle_id, started_at desc)`, `(user_id, client_session_id)` unique, `token_hash` unique.

**Row Level Security:** enable RLS on every table. Policies: users can `select/insert/update/delete` only rows where `user_id = auth.uid()` (and for child tables, where the parent session/vehicle belongs to `auth.uid()`). `shared_reports` is accessible to the public **only through a `SECURITY DEFINER` function** `get_shared_report(token text)` that validates the hashed token, expiry and revocation, increments the view counter, and returns only the permitted fields. No direct anonymous select on any base table.

**Storage:** private buckets `audio`, `sensor-data`, `reports`. Path convention `{user_id}/{vehicle_id}/{session_id}/<file>`. Storage policies restrict access to the owner's folder. Shared reports serve files via short-lived signed URLs created by the backend.

